@startuml virtual_call_flow
' L9 reading page virtual Methods in Depth: how the call vehicle.drive(route) is resolved,
' with vehicle a const Vehicle& to a RoboTaxi. Rendered to ../virtual_call_flow.png at
' 300 dpi on white, with the VS Code extension's plantuml.jar.
!theme mono
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Fira Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam dpi 300
start
:""vehicle.drive(route)""
""vehicle"" is a ""const Vehicle&""
to a ""RoboTaxi"";
if (Is ""drive"" virtual
in ""Vehicle""?) then (no)
  :**Static binding**
The compiler calls the version
of the static type, ""Vehicle"":
""Vehicle::drive"" runs;
else (yes)
  :**Dynamic binding**
1. Read the object's hidden pointer:
it points to ""RoboTaxi""'s vtable;
  :2. Read the ""drive"" entry
of that vtable: ""RoboTaxi::drive"";
  :3. Call it: ""RoboTaxi::drive"" runs;
endif
stop
@enduml
